                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec p \in \mathbb{C}^{n+1}
                      if they differ by multiplication by a complex number of unit norm
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
                      (def.
                      = succeed ")." do
                        %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalProjectiveSpace"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              It is clear that there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              of underlying sets as claimed: Under the equivalence relation defining projective space, every element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec x = (x_1, \cdots, x_{n+1}) \in k^{n+1}
              is equivalent to one of unit norm, namely
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mover
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{\vert \vec x\vert} \vec x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \setminus \{0\}
              of unit norm.
            %p
              It remains to see that this bijection is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{R}
              works verbatim the same, with the evident substitutions.
            %p
              So we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of functions of underlying sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℂ
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo ∖
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi q
                                    %mrow
                                      %msup
                                        %mi S
                                        %mrow
                                          %mn 2
                                          %mi n
                                          %mo +
                                          %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi q
                                    %mrow
                                      %msup
                                        %mi ℂ
                                        %mrow
                                          %mi n
                                          %mo +
                                          %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℂ
                            %msup
                              %mi P
                              %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{2n+1} &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; \mathbb{C}^{n+1} \setminus \{0\}
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{q_{S^{2n+1}}}}\downarrow &amp;\searrow^{\mathrlap{f}}&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{q_{\mathbb{C}^{n+1}}}}
                    \\\
                    S^{2n+1}/S^1 &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \mathbb{C}P^n
                    }
            %p
              where the top horizontal and the two vertical functions are continuous, and where the bottom function is is a bijection. Since the diagonal composite is also continuous, the nature of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space+topology"} quotient space topology
              implies that the bottom function is also continuous. To see that it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              it hence remains to see that it is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+map"} open map
              (by
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "homeomorphism#HomeoContinuousOpenBijection"} this prop.
            %p
              So let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset S^{2n+1}/S^1
              be an open set, which means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi q
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_{S^{2n+1}}^{-1}(U) \subset S^{2n+1}
              is an open set. We need to see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi q
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(q_{S^{2n+1}}^{-1}(U)) \subset \mathbb{C}P^{n}
              is open, hence that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi q
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℂ
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi q
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_{\mathbb{C}^{n+1}}^{-1}(f(q_{S^{2n+1}}^{-1}(U))) \subset \mathbb{C}^{n+1}
              is open. Now by the nature of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
              = succeed "," do
